{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "note": "How the four kits write a DisplayName (the core SDK's projected name, camelCase on the wire: title, lastSender, sender, name) as text: flareDisplayNameText(name, strings). `named` reads its text as it is. `members` joins its names with the locale's separator (zh-CN 、, en-US \", \"), blank names dropped; when total > names + 1 it adds the others, N = total - names - 1 (the reader is a member and is never counted), zh-CN 「等 N 人」, en-US \"and N other(s)\" (the one form at 1); with no name left it reads as an unnamed group. `unnamed` reads by entity: person with an idTail 「用户 <idTail>」/ \"User <idTail>\", person without one 「未知用户」/ \"Unknown user\"; group, system, ai, customer, channel, broadcast and temp their own word, whatever the idTail. The kit writes no id and no shape guess: what the core projected is all it reads. `idTail` is flareIdTail, the rule the core uses to make one and flarePluginFallbackName reads: the id trimmed of surrounding white space, then its last 4 Unicode scalars (not UTF-16 units, not graphemes); a shorter id whole; a blank id the empty string. zh-CN is each kit's default strings, en-US its English preset (Vue: the en-US message tree).",
